{"parentUuid":"e08dd709-0856-45b8-b2c6-80b5d7969606","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cg9oZhTx81vQvR1AkBT5D","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_017pjpAhJZ2yoxHjoSgXLTTu","name":"mcp__claude_ai_Linear__save_comment","input":{"issueId":"COR-2164","body":"## Assessment: real criticals, zero exposure. Recommend sequencing behind COR-2154 rather than patching.\n\n**What it actually is.** \"Benchmark Git tooling\" resolves to **`simple-git`**, reached from the Stage 1b embed server. `npm audit --package-lock-only` on `scripts/bench`:\n\n| Package | Severity | Advisory |\n|---|---|---|\n| `@simple-git/argv-parser` | **critical** | `VISUAL` editor env var omitted from unsafe-editor detection |\n| `simple-git` | **critical** | unsafe-operation guard does not block trailer command configuration |\n| `node-llama-cpp` | high | — |\n\nTotals: 2 critical, 1 high, 0 moderate/low.\n\n**The chain.** `node-llama-cpp` → `simple-git` → `@simple-git/argv-parser`. `node-llama-cpp` is the *only* reason any of this is present; `scripts/bench/package.json` declares it as the sole dependency, for `embed-server.mjs`.\n\n**Exposure: none that I can find.**\n\n- **Never in CI.** No workflow references `scripts/bench`, `embed-server`, or `node-llama-cpp`. Nothing installs this lockfile on a runner.\n- **Never shipped.** It is Node tooling under `scripts/`; it is not in any release build. The product's embedder is a separate Go `staticEmbedder` in `internal/cli/embed.go`, unrelated to this tree.\n- **Local-only, operator-run.** The embed server is Stage 1b benchmark tooling we start by hand. Both advisories need attacker-controlled git config or environment in the repository simple-git operates on — i.e. an attacker already on the machine running the benchmark.\n\nSo the severity is real upstream and the blast radius here is a developer laptop already under the operator's control.\n\n### Why patching is the wrong move\n\n**COR-2154 deletes this entire dependency tree.** It replaces the bundled embedder and RRF with in-process BM25 plus taxonomy filters — and `node-llama-cpp` exists solely to serve that embedder. When COR-2154 lands, `scripts/bench`'s only dependency goes, taking `simple-git` and `@simple-git/argv-parser` with it.\n\nBumping a transitive dep of a package we are about to remove buys nothing and costs a lockfile churn plus a re-verification of the benchmark harness.\n\n**Recommended disposition:** mark this blocked on **COR-2154** (which already has a PR) and re-run `npm audit` afterwards to confirm the tree is gone. If COR-2154 slips or is dropped, revisit — at that point the right fix is upgrading `node-llama-cpp` to a release carrying patched `simple-git`, not pinning the transitive.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3541,"cache_read_input_tokens":861536,"output_tokens":1025,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3541,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1025,"cache_read_input_tokens":861536,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3541,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3541},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_017pjpAhJZ2yoxHjoSgXLTTu":{"issueId":"COR-2164","body":"## Assessment: real criticals, zero exposure. Recommend sequencing behind COR-2154 rather than patching.\n\n**What it actually is.** \"Benchmark Git tooling\" resolves to **`simple-git`**, reached from the Stage 1b embed server. `npm audit --package-lock-only` on `scripts/bench`:\n\n| Package | Severity | Advisory |\n|---|---|---|\n| `@simple-git/argv-parser` | **critical** | `VISUAL` editor env var omitted from unsafe-editor detection |\n| `simple-git` | **critical** | unsafe-operation guard does not block trailer command configuration |\n| `node-llama-cpp` | high | — |\n\nTotals: 2 critical, 1 high, 0 moderate/low.\n\n**The chain.** `node-llama-cpp` → `simple-git` → `@simple-git/argv-parser`. `node-llama-cpp` is the *only* reason any of this is present; `scripts/bench/package.json` declares it as the sole dependency, for `embed-server.mjs`.\n\n**Exposure: none that I can find.**\n\n- **Never in CI.** No workflow references `scripts/bench`, `embed-server`, or `node-llama-cpp`. Nothing installs this lockfile on a runner.\n- **Never shipped.** It is Node tooling under `scripts/`; it is not in any release build. The product's embedder is a separate Go `staticEmbedder` in `internal/cli/embed.go`, unrelated to this tree.\n- **Local-only, operator-run.** The embed server is Stage 1b benchmark tooling we start by hand. Both advisories need attacker-controlled git config or environment in the repository simple-git operates on — i.e. an attacker already on the machine running the benchmark.\n\nSo the severity is real upstream and the blast radius here is a developer laptop already under the operator's control.\n\n### Why patching is the wrong move\n\n**COR-2154 deletes this entire dependency tree.** It replaces the bundled embedder and RRF with in-process BM25 plus taxonomy filters — and `node-llama-cpp` exists solely to serve that embedder. When COR-2154 lands, `scripts/bench`'s only dependency goes, taking `simple-git` and `@simple-git/argv-parser` with it.\n\nBumping a transitive dep of a package we are about to remove buys nothing and costs a lockfile churn plus a re-verification of the benchmark harness.\n\n**Recommended disposition:** mark this blocked on **COR-2154** (which already has a PR) and re-run `npm audit` afterwards to confirm the tree is gone. If COR-2154 slips or is dropped, revisit — at that point the right fix is upgrading `node-llama-cpp` to a release carrying patched `simple-git`, not pinning the transitive.\n"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"6023fffc-973c-4743-8434-9246cd96bae8","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Cg9oZgoGPisG2cEZVV8j2","requestRef":"04d7e3d2-6456-4e3e-8780-2bf410e63adf","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5[1m]","attributionMcpServer":"claude.ai Linear","attributionMcpTool":"save_comment","type":"assistant","uuid":"7e55b313-512a-4aaf-8459-337db935c1a7","timestamp":"2026-10-18T13:45:33.148Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"60a744a6-1b89-494f-a7de-f94ff9566958","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-rebase","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","version":"2.1.301","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floofy-discovering-bachman"}
{"parentUuid":"7e55b313-512a-4aaf-8459-337db935c1a7","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"effeb2d1-329d-425b-9549-b5199a46d687","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017pjpAhJZ2yoxHjoSgXLTTu","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"id\":\"cbc63fb9-9078-4fea-b61c-fd516507a960\",\"body\":\"## Assessment: real criticals, zero exposure. Recommend sequencing behind COR-2154 rather than patching.\\n\\n**What it actually is.** \\\"Benchmark Git tooling\\\" resolves to **`simple-git`**, reached from the Stage 1b embed server. `npm audit --package-lock-only` on `scripts/bench`:\\n\\n| Package | Severity | Advisory |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| `@simple-git/argv-parser` | **critical** | `VISUAL` editor env var omitted from unsafe-editor detection |\\n| `simple-git` | **critical** | unsafe-operation guard does not block trailer command configuration |\\n| `node-llama-cpp` | high | — |\\n\\nTotals: 2 critical, 1 high, 0 moderate/low.\\n\\n**The chain.** `node-llama-cpp` → `simple-git` → `@simple-git/argv-parser`. `node-llama-cpp` is the *only* reason any of this is present; `scripts/bench/package.json` declares it as the sole dependency, for `embed-server.mjs`.\\n\\n**Exposure: none that I can find.**\\n\\n- **Never in CI.** No workflow references `scripts/bench`, `embed-server`, or `node-llama-cpp`. Nothing installs this lockfile on a runner.\\n- **Never shipped.** It is Node tooling under `scripts/`; it is not in any release build. The product's embedder is a separate Go `staticEmbedder` in `internal/cli/embed.go`, unrelated to this tree.\\n- **Local-only, operator-run.** The embed server is Stage 1b benchmark tooling we start by hand. Both advisories need attacker-controlled git config or environment in the repository simple-git operates on — i.e. an attacker already on the machine running the benchmark.\\n\\nSo the severity is real upstream and the blast radius here is a developer laptop already under the operator's control.\\n\\n### Why patching is the wrong move\\n\\n**COR-2154 deletes this entire dependency tree.** It replaces the bundled embedder and RRF with in-process BM25 plus taxonomy filters — and `node-llama-cpp` exists solely to serve that embedder. When COR-2154 lands, `scripts/bench`'s only dependency goes, taking `simple-git` and `@simple-git/argv-parser` with it.\\n\\nBumping a transitive dep of a package we are about to remove buys nothing and costs a lockfile churn plus a re-verification of the benchmark harness.\\n\\n**Recommended disposition:** mark this blocked on **COR-2154** (which already has a PR) and re-run `npm audit` afterwards to confirm the tree is gone. If COR-2154 slips or is dropped, revisit — at that point the right fix is upgrading `node-llama-cpp` to a release carrying patched `simple-git`, not pinning the transitive.\\n\",\"attachments\":[],\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-18T13:45:34.203Z\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-18T13:45:34.108Z\",\"parentId\":null,\"resolvedAt\":null,\"quotedText\":null,\"author\":{\"id\":\"383d093a-5c76-4a6c-9c2b-660b61ca3f3d\",\"name\":\"Suhaan Thayyil\"},\"onBehalfOf\":null}"}]}]},"uuid":"21100d84-3945-47fc-8480-af5d631d9f36","timestamp":"2026-10-18T13:45:34.379Z","toolUseResult":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"id\":\"cbc63fb9-9078-4fea-b61c-fd516507a960\",\"body\":\"## Assessment: real criticals, zero exposure. Recommend sequencing behind COR-2154 rather than patching.\\n\\n**What it actually is.** \\\"Benchmark Git tooling\\\" resolves to **`simple-git`**, reached from the Stage 1b embed server. `npm audit --package-lock-only` on `scripts/bench`:\\n\\n| Package | Severity | Advisory |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| `@simple-git/argv-parser` | **critical** | `VISUAL` editor env var omitted from unsafe-editor detection |\\n| `simple-git` | **critical** | unsafe-operation guard does not block trailer command configuration |\\n| `node-llama-cpp` | high | — |\\n\\nTotals: 2 critical, 1 high, 0 moderate/low.\\n\\n**The chain.** `node-llama-cpp` → `simple-git` → `@simple-git/argv-parser`. `node-llama-cpp` is the *only* reason any of this is present; `scripts/bench/package.json` declares it as the sole dependency, for `embed-server.mjs`.\\n\\n**Exposure: none that I can find.**\\n\\n- **Never in CI.** No workflow references `scripts/bench`, `embed-server`, or `node-llama-cpp`. Nothing installs this lockfile on a runner.\\n- **Never shipped.** It is Node tooling under `scripts/`; it is not in any release build. The product's embedder is a separate Go `staticEmbedder` in `internal/cli/embed.go`, unrelated to this tree.\\n- **Local-only, operator-run.** The embed server is Stage 1b benchmark tooling we start by hand. Both advisories need attacker-controlled git config or environment in the repository simple-git operates on — i.e. an attacker already on the machine running the benchmark.\\n\\nSo the severity is real upstream and the blast radius here is a developer laptop already under the operator's control.\\n\\n### Why patching is the wrong move\\n\\n**COR-2154 deletes this entire dependency tree.** It replaces the bundled embedder and RRF with in-process BM25 plus taxonomy filters — and `node-llama-cpp` exists solely to serve that embedder. When COR-2154 lands, `scripts/bench`'s only dependency goes, taking `simple-git` and `@simple-git/argv-parser` with it.\\n\\nBumping a transitive dep of a package we are about to remove buys nothing and costs a lockfile churn plus a re-verification of the benchmark harness.\\n\\n**Recommended disposition:** mark this blocked on **COR-2154** (which already has a PR) and re-run `npm audit` afterwards to confirm the tree is gone. If COR-2154 slips or is dropped, revisit — at that point the right fix is upgrading `node-llama-cpp` to a release carrying patched `simple-git`, not pinning the transitive.\\n\",\"attachments\":[],\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-18T13:45:34.203Z\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-18T13:45:34.108Z\",\"parentId\":null,\"resolvedAt\":null,\"quotedText\":null,\"author\":{\"id\":\"383d093a-5