{"parentUuid":"03195135-0daa-4d9f-b96c-9001bc6666a5","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"effeb2d1-329d-425b-9549-b5199a46d687","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01T6A4oEayqB4BfYA3jwqm9m","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"id\":\"COR-2156\",\"uuid\":\"7e50fbc0-0d29-430b-b4a2-02f8ae07c4ce\",\"title\":\"Brain's Git reads must not lock the user's shared index\",\"description\":\"Brain's read-only Git subprocesses refreshed and **locked the shared index**, so a background brief could block the user's own `git` commands in the same repo.\\n\\nFix: pass `--no-optional-locks`, and use `git diff-index --shortstat HEAD` for the brief's diff summary to avoid the remaining `git diff` index refresh. Both invocations and the resulting diff stat are pinned in regression tests.\\n\\n**PR:** [#367](<https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/367>) — mergeable, **0 failing checks**\\n\\n## Known limit worth encoding in the test\\n\\n`--no-optional-locks` stops `git status` but **not** `git diff <commit>`. If a future read needs that form, the durable fix is `GIT_INDEX_FILE` pointed at a copy, which keeps both the answer and the lock-freedom.\",\"projectMilestone\":{\"id\":\"bc05f7ea-a603-4d11-bcdc-d9ef4afb9d74\",\"name\":\"M2 Close the brain blockers\"},\"priority\":{\"value\":0,\"name\":\"No priority\"},\"url\":\"https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-2156/brains-git-reads-must-not-lock-the-users-shared-index\",\"gitBranchName\":\"suhaan/cor-2156-brains-git-reads-must-not-lock-the-users-shared-index\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-16T01:09:46.045Z\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-16T03:01:26.977Z\",\"archivedAt\":null,\"completedAt\":null,\"startedAt\":null,\"canceledAt\":null,\"dueDate\":null,\"slaStartedAt\":null,\"slaMediumRiskAt\":null,\"slaHighRiskAt\":null,\"slaBreachesAt\":null,\"status\":\"Backlog\",\"statusType\":\"backlog\",\"labels\":[],\"attachments\":[],\"documents\":[],\"stateHistory\":[{\"state\":{\"id\":\"6170bf77-16d7-4d42-9fe6-e0090e8536a0\",\"name\":\"Backlog\",\"type\":\"backlog\"},\"startedAt\":\"2026-10-16T01:09:46.045Z\",\"endedAt\":null}],\"createdBy\":\"Suhaan Thayyil\",\"createdById\":\"383d093a-5c76-4a6c-9c2b-660b61ca3f3d\",\"project\":\"P0 · GA the Local Brain\",\"projectId\":\"91954c69-3fab-4281-84e0-cf4b81d85d75\",\"team\":\"Core\",\"teamId\":\"894690b6-2173-4cbe-abd3-6e7ea5ff5bb9\"}"}]}]},"uuid":"59283c81-a71d-45bf-82e6-a5c80c6d2d90","timestamp":"2026-10-18T13:46:45.938Z","toolUseResult":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"id\":\"COR-2156\",\"uuid\":\"7e50fbc0-0d29-430b-b4a2-02f8ae07c4ce\",\"title\":\"Brain's Git reads must not lock the user's shared index\",\"description\":\"Brain's read-only Git subprocesses refreshed and **locked the shared index**, so a background brief could block the user's own `git` commands in the same repo.\\n\\nFix: pass `--no-optional-locks`, and use `git diff-index --shortstat HEAD` for the brief's diff summary to avoid the remaining `git diff` index refresh. Both invocations and the resulting diff stat are pinned in regression tests.\\n\\n**PR:** [#367](<https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/367>) — mergeable, **0 failing checks**\\n\\n## Known limit worth encoding in the test\\n\\n`--no-optional-locks` stops `git status` but **not** `git diff <commit>`. If a future read needs that form, the durable fix is `GIT_INDEX_FILE` pointed at a copy, which keeps both the answer and the lock-freedom.\",\"projectMilestone\":{\"id\":\"bc05f7ea-a603-4d11-bcdc-d9ef4afb9d74\",\"name\":\"M2 Close the brain blockers\"},\"priority\":{\"value\":0,\"name\":\"No priority\"},\"url\":\"https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-2156/brains-git-reads-must-not-lock-the-users-shared-index\",\"gitBranchName\":\"suhaan/cor-2156-brains-git-reads-must-not-lock-the-users-shared-index\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-16T01:09:46.045Z\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-16T03:01:26.977Z\",\"archivedAt\":null,\"completedAt\":null,\"startedAt\":null,\"canceledAt\":null,\"dueDate\":null,\"slaStar