{"parentUuid":"347ddfec-9d7e-474c-a63a-703df676a000","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"file","filename":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-relnotes/internal/setupui/consent.go","content":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-relnotes/internal/setupui/consent.go","content":"package setupui\n\nimport (\n\t\"bufio\"\n\t\"fmt\"\n\t\"io\"\n\t\"strings\"\n)\n\n// consent.go is phase 4's gate. Distilling sessions into durable facts is the\n// only part of setup that spends money, and until this file existed it was\n// opt-OUT: a first run distilled unless the operator happened to know about\n// --no-backfill.\n//\n// Two properties matter more than the wording:\n//\n//   - DEFAULT NO. Bare Enter, EOF, a closed stdin, garbage twice: all skip.\n//     Silence is never consent to spend.\n//   - NEVER BLOCK WITHOUT A TERMINAL. A prompt in CI is a wedged pipeline, and\n//     a wedged pipeline is a worse outcome than any amount of unspent budget.\n//     The no-TTY path does not read stdin AT ALL — not a byte, not a peek —\n//     which is a stronger and far more testable claim than \"it defaults\".\n\n// Override is an explicit instruction from a flag, which suppresses the prompt.\ntype Override int\n\nconst (\n\t// OverrideNone leaves the decision to the prompt.\n\tOverrideNone Override = iota\n\t// OverrideYes is --yes: the only way to spend without a human.\n\tOverrideYes\n\t// OverrideNo is --no-backfill.\n\tOverrideNo\n)\n\n// ConsentRequest is everything the gate needs. It carries the TTY capability\n// explicitly rather than sniffing a file descriptor, so every path through\n// this function is reachable from a unit test.\ntype ConsentRequest struct {\n\t// Sessions is how many sessions could be distilled.\n\tSessions int\n\t// Agent is the agent CLI that would run. Empty means none was found.\n\tAgent string\n\t// Model and Effort qualify the agent, for the informed-decision line.\n\tModel  string\n\tEffort string\n\t// Override is the flag, if one was passed.\n\tOverride Override\n\t// TTY reports whether a human can answer.\n\tTTY bool\n\t// ResumeCommand is the one command that starts a distill later. It is\n\t// printed on every skip, because a skip that does not say how to change\n\t// its mind is a dead end.\n\tResumeCommand string\n}\n\n// ConsentReason is WHY consent landed where it did, as a value.\n//\n// Reason below is a sentence for a human. Anything that needs to branch on the\n// outcome must branch on this instead: the short form has to tell \"no agent on\n// PATH\" apart from \"the human said no\", and deriving that by matching English\n// against Reason breaks the moment the sentence is reworded.\ntype ConsentReason int\n\nconst (\n\t// ConsentReasonUnset is the zero value; treat it as \"not decided here\".\n\tConsentReasonUnset ConsentReason = iota\n\t// ConsentReasonNoBackfill is --no-backfill.\n\tConsentReasonNoBackfill\n\t// ConsentReasonNoSessions is a repo with nothing recorded yet.\n\tConsentReasonNoSessions\n\t// ConsentReasonNoAgent is sessions present and no CLI able to read them.\n\tConsentReasonNoAgent\n\t// ConsentReasonFlagYes is --yes.\n\tConsentReasonFlagYes\n\t// ConsentReasonNoTTY is a non-interactive stdin, where silence is not\n\t// consent.\n\tConsentReasonNoTTY\n\t// ConsentReasonAccepted is a human who answered yes.\n\tConsentReasonAccepted\n\t// ConsentReasonDeclined is a human who answered no.\n\tConsentReasonDeclined\n\n\t// The four below are reached BEFORE consent is asked, so they are not\n\t// consent decisions at all -- they are the reasons the question never\n\t// came up. They live in this enum because the short form needs one typed\n\t// answer to \"why was nothing distilled\", and inventing a second enum for\n\t// half of it would just move the matching problem.\n\n\t// ConsentReasonPaused is `brain stop`: background work is paused, and\n\t// re-running setup will skip again. The remedy is `start`.\n\tConsentReasonPaused\n\t// ConsentReasonAlreadyDistilled is a re-run with nothing pending.\n\tConsentReasonAlreadyDistilled\n\t// ConsentReasonAlreadyRunning is a backfill already in flight. Reporting\n\t// this as \"skipped\" contradicts the machine's actual state.\n\tConsentReasonAlreadyRunning\n\t// ConsentReasonNoExecutable is an unresolvable path to this binary, so\n\t// nothing could be spawned.\n\tConsentReasonNoExecutable\n)\n\n// ConsentOutcome is the decision and why it was reached.\ntype ConsentOutcome struct {\n\t// Spend is the answer.\n\tSpend bool\n\t// Reason is always set, including when Spend is true. It is what the\n\t// settled phase line says.\n\tReason string\n\t// Why is the same decision as a value, for callers that must branch.\n\tWhy ConsentReason\n\t// Prompted reports whether a human was actually asked. A test asserting\n\t// \"CI does not block\" asserts on this, not on the answer.\n\tPrompted bool\n}\n\n// DefaultResumeCommand is the command printed when a distill is skipped.\nconst DefaultResumeCommand = \"entire brain distill\"\n\n// Consent decides whether phase 4 may spend.\n//\n// Order is load bearing. The three \"spending is impossible\" checks come first,\n// so --yes in a repo with no sessions and no agent reports the truth instead of\n// claiming it spent. Then the flags, then the terminal. The reader `in` is\n// touched on exactly one path: a real prompt on a real terminal.\nfunc Consent(req ConsentRequest, in io.Reader, out io.Writer, r *Renderer) ConsentOutcome {\n\tresume := req.ResumeCommand\n\tif strings.TrimSpace(resume) == \"\" {\n\t\tresume = DefaultResumeCommand\n\t}\n\n\tswitch {\n\t// Nothing to distill comes FIRST, ahead of --no-backfill. The flag\n\t// declines work; it cannot decline work that does not exist, and saying\n\t// \"not distilled (--no-backfill)\" to someone whose repo has no captured\n\t// sessions reports a decision instead of explaining the state. The state\n\t// is that there is nothing here yet, and that is not a problem -- it is\n\t// what every repository looks like before its first agent session.\n\tcase req.Sessions <= 0:\n\t\treturn ConsentOutcome{Reason: \"no sessions to distill; the brain is queryable now\", Why: ConsentReasonNoSessions}\n\tcase req.Override == OverrideNo:\n\t\treturn ConsentOutcome{Reason: \"not distilled (--no-backfill); start later: \" + resume, Why: ConsentReasonNoBackfill}\n\tcase req.Agent == \"\":\n\t\treturn ConsentOutcome{Reason: \"no agent CLI on PATH, nothing can distill; \" + RemedyAgent, Why: ConsentReasonNoAgent}\n\tcase req.Override == OverrideYes:\n\t\treturn ConsentOutcome{Spend: true, Reason: \"distilling \" + plural(req.Sessions, \"session\") + \" (--yes)\", Why: ConsentReasonFlagYes}\n\tcase !req.TTY:\n\t\t// Not a prompt, not a read, not a wait: one line and a default.\n\t\treturn ConsentOutcome{Reason: \"not distilled: no terminal to ask, and silence is not consent; run \" + resume + \" or pass --yes\", Why: ConsentReasonNoTTY}\n\t}\n\n\twritePrompt(out, r, req)\n\tanswer, prompted := askTwice(in, out, r)\n\tif answer {\n\t\treturn ConsentOutcome{Spend: true, Reason: \"distilling \" + plural(req.Sessions, \"session\") + \", newest first\", Why: ConsentReasonAccepted, Prompted: prompted}\n\t}\n\treturn ConsentOutcome{Reason: \"not distilled; the brain is queryable now, start later: \" + resume, Why: ConsentReasonDeclined, Prompted: prompted}\n}\n\n// writePrompt paints the block the operator is answering. It uses the same\n// gutter as every phase line, with the glyph column left blank: a question is\n// not an outcome and must not wear an outcome's tick.\nfunc writePrompt(out io.Writer, r *Renderer, req ConsentRequest) {\n\tif out == nil {\n\t\treturn\n\t}\n\tbullet := \" \" + r.Bullet() + \" \"\n\tagent := \"Agent: \" + req.Agent\n\tif req.Model != \"\" {\n\t\tagent += bullet + \"model: \" + req.Model\n\t}\n\tif req.Effort != \"\" {\n\t\tagent += bullet + \"effort: \" + req.Effort\n\t}\n\tlines := []Line{\n\t\t{Title: PhaseFacts.Title(), Text: plural(req.Sessions, \"session\") + \" can be distilled into durable facts.\", Accent: PhaseFacts.Accent()},\n\t\t{Text: agent, Accent: PhaseFacts.Accent()},\n\t\t{Text: \"Estimated: ~\" + plural(req.Sessions, \"agent call\") + \", newest first, resumable.\", Accent: PhaseFacts.Accent()},\n\t\t{Blank: true},\n\t}\n\tfor _, line := range lines {\n\t\tfmt.Fprintln(out, r.Line(line))\n\t}\n}\n\n// question is the prompt itself. \"[y/N]\" is not decoration: the capital is the\n// default, and it is the default.\nconst question = \"Distill now? [y/N]\"\n\n// askTwice reads an answer, re-asking ONCE on something unrecognisable and\n// defaulting to No after that. Two chances is the whole budget: a loop here is\n// a different way of blocking a pipeline.\nfunc askTwice(in io.Reader, out io.Writer, r *Renderer) (bool, bool) {\n\tif in == nil {\n\t\treturn false, false\n\t}\n\treader := bufio.NewReader(in)\n\tfor attempt := 0; attempt < 2; attempt++ {\n\t\t// Printed with a trailing space Line would have trimmed: the cursor has to\n\t\t// sit clear of the \"]\" or the answer reads as part of the question.\n\t\tfmt.Fprint(out, r.Line(Line{Text: question, Accent: PhaseFacts.Accent()})+\" \")\n\t\tline, err := reader.ReadString('\\n')\n\t\tanswer := strings.ToLower(strings.TrimSpace(line))\n\t\tif err != nil && answer == \"\" {\n\t\t\t// EOF, a closed stdin, an interrupt that shut the pipe: No, with a\n\t\t\t// newline so the next line does not land beside the prompt.\n\t\t\tfmt.Fprintln(out)\n\t\t\treturn false, true\n\t\t}\n\t\tswitch answer {\n\t\tcase \"y\", \"yes\":\n\t\t\treturn true, true\n\t\tcase \"\", \"n\", \"no\":\n\t\t\treturn false, true\n\t\t}\n\t\tif attempt == 0 {\n\t\t\tfmt.Fprintln(out, r.Line(Line{Text: \"Please answer y or n.\", Accent: PhaseFacts.Accent()}))\n\t\t}\n\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\tfmt.Fprintln(out)\n\t\t\treturn false, true\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\treturn false, true\n}\n","numLines":226,"startLine":1,"totalLines":226}},"displayPath":"../brain-relnotes/internal/setupui/consent.go"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"c1b0d6aa-29be-40d6-be7c-6dea73262474","timestamp":"2026-10-18T20:25:31.687Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nCalled the Read tool with the following input: {\"file_path\":\"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-relnotes/internal/setupui/consent.go\"}\n</system-reminder>"},{"content":"<system-reminder>\nResult of calling the Read tool:\n1\tpackage setupui\n2\t\n3\timport (\n4\t\t\"bufio\"\n5\t\t\"fmt\"\n6\t\t\"io\"\n7\t\t\"strings\"\n8\t)\n9\t\n10\t// consent.go is phase 4's gate. Distilling sessions into durable facts is the\n11\t// only part of setup that spends money, and until this file existed it was\n12\t// opt-OUT: a first run distilled unless the operator happened to know about\n13\t// --no-backfill.\n14\t//\n15\t// Two properties matter more than the wording:\n16\t//\n17\t//   - DEFAULT NO. Bare Enter, EOF, a closed stdin, garbage twice: all skip.\n18\t//     Silence is never consent to spend.\n19\t//   - NEVER BLOCK WITHOUT A TERMINAL. A prompt in CI is a wedged pipeline, and\n20\t//     a wedged pipeline is a worse outcome than any amount of unspent budget.\n21\t//     The no-TTY path does not read stdin AT ALL — not a byte, not a peek —\n22\t//     which is a stronger and far more testable claim than \"it defaults\".\n23\t\n24\t// Override is an explicit instruction from a flag, which suppresses the prompt.\n25\ttype Override int\n26\t\n27\tconst (\n28\t\t// OverrideNone leaves the decision to the prompt.\n29\t\tOverrideNone Override = iota\n30\t\t// OverrideYes is --yes: the only way to spend without a human.\n31\t\tOverrideYes\n32\t\t// OverrideNo is --no-backfill.\n33\t\tOverrideNo\n34\t)\n35\t\n36\t// ConsentRequest is everything the gate needs. It carries the TTY capability\n37\t// explicitly rather than sniffing a file descriptor, so every path through\n38\t// this function is reachable from a unit test.\n39\ttype ConsentRequest struct {\n40\t\t// Sessions is how many sessions could be distilled.\n41\t\tSessions int\n42\t\t// Agent is the agent CLI that would run. Empty means none was found.\n43\t\tAgent string\n44\t\t// Model and Effort qualify the agent, for the informed-decision line.\n45\t\tModel  string\n46\t\tEffort string\n47\t\t// Override is the flag, if one was passed.\n48\t\tOverride Override\n49\t\t// TTY reports whether a human can answer.\n50\t\tTTY bool\n51\t\t// ResumeCommand is the one command that starts a distill later. It is\n52\t\t// printed on every skip, because a skip that does not say how to change\n53\t\t// its mind is a dead end.\n54\t\tResumeCommand string\n55\t}\n56\t\n57\t// ConsentReason is WHY consent landed where it did, as a value.\n58\t//\n59\t// Reason below is a sentence for a human. Anything that needs to branch on the\n60\t// outcome must branch on this instead: the short form has to tell \"no agent on\n61\t// PATH\" apart from \"the human said no\", and deriving that by matching English\n62\t// against Reason breaks the moment the sentence is reworded.\n63\ttype ConsentReason int\n64\t\n65\tconst (\n66\t\t// ConsentReasonUnset is the zero value; treat it as \"not decided here\".\n67\t\tConsentReasonUnset ConsentReason = iota\n68\t\t// ConsentReasonNoBackfill is --no-backfill.\n69\t\tConsentReasonNoBackfill\n70\t\t// ConsentReasonNoSessions is a repo with nothing recorded yet.\n71\t\tConsentReasonNoSessions\n72\t\t// ConsentReasonNoAgent is sessions present and no CLI able to read them.\n73\t\tConsentReasonNoAgent\n74\t\t// ConsentReasonFlagYes is --yes.\n75\t\tConsentReasonFlagYes\n76\t\t// ConsentReasonNoTTY is a non-interactive stdin, where silence is not\n77\t\t// consent.\n78\t\tConsentReasonNoTTY\n79\t\t// ConsentReasonAccepted is a human who answered yes.\n80\t\tConsentReasonAccepted\n81\t\t// ConsentReasonDeclined is a human who answered no.\n82\t\tConsentReasonDeclined\n83\t\n84\t\t// The four below are reached BEFORE consent is asked, so they are not\n85\t\t// consent decisions at all -- they are the reasons the question never\n86\t\t// came up. They live in this enum because the short form needs one typed\n87\t\t// answer to \"why was nothing distilled\", and inventing a second enum for\n88\t\t// half of it would just move the matching problem.\n89\t\n90\t\t// ConsentReasonPaused is `brain stop`: background work is paused, and\n91\t\t// re-running setup will skip again. The remedy is `start`.\n92\t\tConsentReasonPaused\n93\t\t// ConsentReasonAlreadyDistilled is a re-run with nothing pending.\n94\t\tConsentReasonAlreadyDistilled\n95\t\t// ConsentReasonAlreadyRunning is a backfill already in flight. Reporting\n96\t\t// this as \"skipped\" contradicts the machine's actual state.\n97\t\tConsentReasonAlreadyRunning\n98\t\t// ConsentReasonNoExecutable is an unresolvable path to this binary, so\n99\t\t// nothing could be spawned.\n100\t\tConsentReasonNoExecutable\n101\t)\n102\t\n103\t// ConsentOutcome is the decision and why it was reached.\n104\ttype ConsentOutcome struct {\n105\t\t// Spend is the answer.\n106\t\tSpend bool\n107\t\t// Reason is always set, including when Spend is true. It is what the\n108\t\t// settled phase line says.\n109\t\tReason string\n110\t\t// Why is the same decision as a value, for callers that must branch.\n111\t\tWhy ConsentReason\n112\t\t// Prompted reports whether a human was actually asked. A test asserting\n113\t\t// \"CI does not block\" asserts on this, not on the answer.\n114\t\tPrompted bool\n115\t}\n116\t\n117\t// DefaultResumeCommand is the command printed when a distill is skipped.\n118\tconst DefaultResumeCommand = \"entire brain distill\"\n119\t\n120\t// Consent decides whether phase 4 may spend.\n121\t//\n122\t// Order is load bearing. The three \"spending is impossible\" checks come first,\n123\t// so --yes in a repo with no sessions and no agent reports the truth instead of\n124\t// claiming it spent. Then the flags, then the terminal. The reader `in` is\n125\t// touched on exactly one path: a real prompt on a real terminal.\n126\tfunc Consent(r