 a single step. So a\n huge or deliberately hostile repo could keep entire graph busy\n for a very long time. That's a denial-of-service risk.ashtom  [7:42 AM]\nBrain's file-anchor extraction cuts hyphenated paths into fragments: pre-build.ts also yields website/scripts/pre and build.ts. My first attempt was anchored only to those broken pieces, so I recorded the fact again with the full paths in backticks and retracted the two earlier versions. The fragments still appear next to the correct paths, because the extractor always produces them. A recall on main now returns just the one active fact.[7:42 AM]This sounds like a bug? pre-build.ts is a file in our entire.io repo\n</pasted_content id=\"ecd9\">\n\n| either way fix it and resolve it and before all this give me a message like this| for last week,\n\n<pasted_content id=\"ecd9\">\nEvis  [12:47 AM]\ntoday:\n\nfocused on implementing state model (still more work to do but in a better spot)\nworking on cleaning up distill pipeline\nupdating brainstore to work with new anchors\n\n\nentire-brain\n• :merged: Unified hosted state model — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/303\n• :merged: Kill switch canonicalized as NO_EGRESS — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/301\n• :merged: Anchors stamp commit and session — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/302\n• :merged: Pre-push hook replaces checkpoint event — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/300\n• :merged: Per-chunk distill cache for transcripts — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/293\n• :merged: Earlier pre-push hook attempt, closed — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/299\n• :merged: Hosted sync now opt-in only — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/292\n• :merged: Tests drop per-test codex builds — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/298\n• :merged: Hosted runners moved to Depot — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/295\n\ncli\n• :merged: Detached child drops parent pipes — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1586\n• :merged: Detached checkpoint hint from PostCommit — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1581\n</pasted_content id=\"ecd9\">\n\n||| not all ahs to be :mergred can be :review too if not and mapp erpsitve linear to trails, no more prs\n"},{"type":"text","text":"<local-command-caveat>The command below was run directly in Claude Code, not sent to you as a request, and its output goes straight to the user. It's recorded here as context for later messages.</local-command-caveat>\n"},{"type":"text","text":"<command-name>/login</command-name>\n            <command-message>login</command-message>\n            <command-args></command-args>\n"},{"type":"text","text":"<local-command-stdout>Login successful</local-command-stdout>\n"},{"type":"text","text":"are these tow thigns related; i care ab tthe bottom issue;\n\n<pasted_content id=\"ecd9\">\nashtom  [9:27 AM]\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-graph/trails/102/fix-sem-cli-enforce-a-wall-clock-ceiling-on-indexing - did you see my comment? what did you build this for?\nSuhaan  [10:59 AM]\nThis is from august, when the focus was mainly on graph, this PR was to fix a security finding that my agent found in the security loop\nindexing had no time limit. Some steps get roughly\nquadratically slower as files grow; for example, one\n16,000-symbol TypeScript file took 21.7s in a single step. So a\n huge or deliberately hostile repo could keep entire graph busy\n for a very long time. That's a denial-of-service risk.ashtom  [7:42 AM]\nBrain's file-anchor extraction cuts hyphenated paths into fragments: pre-build.ts also yields website/scripts/pre and build.ts. My first attempt was anchored only to those broken pieces, so I recorded the fact again with the full paths in backticks and retracted the two earlier versions. The fragments still appear next to the correct paths, because the extractor always produces them. A recall on main now returns just the one active fact.[7:42 AM]This sounds like a bug? pre-build.ts is a file in our entire.io repo\n</pasted_content id=\"ecd9\">\n\n| either way fix it and resolve it and before all this give me a message like this| for last week,\n\n<pasted_content id=\"ecd9\">\nEvis  [12:47 AM]\ntoday:\n\nfocused on implementing state model (still more work to do but in a better spot)\nworking on cleaning up distill pipeline\nupdating brainstore to work with new anchors\n\n\nentire-brain\n• :merged: Unified hosted state model — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/303\n• :merged: Kill switch canonicalized as NO_EGRESS — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/301\n• :merged: Anchors stamp commit and session — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/302\n• :merged: Pre-push hook replaces checkpoint event — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/300\n• :merged: Per-chunk distill cache for transcripts — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/293\n• :merged: Earlier pre-push hook attempt, closed — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/299\n• :merged: Hosted sync now opt-in only — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/292\n• :merged: Tests drop per-test codex builds — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/298\n• :merged: Hosted runners moved to Depot — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/295\n\ncli\n• :merged: Detached child drops parent pipes — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1586\n• :merged: Detached checkpoint hint from PostCommit — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1581\n</pasted_content id=\"ecd9\">\n\n||| not all ahs to be :mergred can be :review too if not and mapp erpsitve linear to trails, no more prs"}]}}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","hash":"17cbc6b90289742ab4231dea1c54dd32fc2872978f657348446feacd15455a3d","message":{"role":"system","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Called the Read tool with the following input: {\"file_path\":\"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-relnotes/internal/setupui/consent.go\"}\nResult of calling the Read tool:\n1\tpackage setupui\n2\t\n3\timport (\n4\t\t\"bufio\"\n5\t\t\"fmt\"\n6\t\t\"io\"\n7\t\t\"strings\"\n8\t)\n9\t\n10\t// consent.go is phase 4's gate. Distilling sessions into durable facts is the\n11\t// only part of setup that spends money, and until this file existed it was\n12\t// opt-OUT: a first run distilled unless the operator happened to know about\n13\t// --no-backfill.\n14\t//\n15\t// Two properties matter more than the wording:\n16\t//\n17\t//   - DEFAULT NO. Bare Enter, EOF, a closed stdin, garbage twice: all skip.\n18\t//     Silence is never consent to spend.\n19\t//   - NEVER BLOCK WITHOUT A TERMINAL. A prompt in CI is a wedged pipeline, and\n20\t//     a wedged pipeline is a worse outcome than any amount of unspent budget.\n21\t//     The no-TTY path does not read stdin AT ALL — not a byte, not a peek —\n22\t//     which is a stronger and far more testable claim than \"it defaults\".\n23\t\n24\t// Override is an explicit instruction from a flag, which suppresses the prompt.\n25\ttype Override int\n26\t\n27\tconst (\n28\t\t// OverrideNone leaves the decision to the prompt.\n29\t\tOverrideNone Override = iota\n30\t\t// OverrideYes is --yes: the only way to spend without a human.\n31\t\tOverrideYes\n32\t\t// OverrideNo is --no-backfill.\n33\t\tOverrideNo\n34\t)\n35\t\n36\t// ConsentRequest is everything the gate needs. It carries the TTY capability\n37\t// explicitly rather than sniffing a file descriptor, so every path through\n38\t// this function is reachable from a unit test.\n39\ttype ConsentRequest struct {\n40\t\t// Sessions is how many sessions could be distilled.\n41\t\tSessions int\n42\t\t// Agent is the agent CLI that would run. Empty means none was found.\n43\t\tAgent string\n44\t\t// Model and Effort qualify the agent, for the informed-decision line.\n45\t\tModel  string\n46\t\tEffort string\n47\t\t// Override is the flag, if one was passed.\n48\t\tOverride Override\n49\t\t// TTY reports whether a human can answer.\n50\t\tTTY bool\n51\t\t// ResumeCommand is the one command that starts a distill later. It is\n52\t\t// printed on every skip, because a skip that does not say how to change\n53\t\t// its mind is a dead end.\n54\t\tResumeCommand string\n55\t}\n56\t\n57\t// ConsentReason is WHY consent landed where it did, as a value.\n58\t//\n59\t// Reason below is a sentence for a human. Anything that needs to branch on the\n60\t// outcome must branch on this instead: the short form has to tell \"no agent on\n61\t// PATH\" apart from \"the human said no\", and deriving that by matching English\n62\t// against Reason breaks the moment the sentence is reworded.\n63\ttype ConsentReason int\n64\t\n65\tconst (\n66\t\t// ConsentReasonUnset is the zero value; treat it as \"not decided here\".\n67\t\tConsentReasonUnset ConsentReason = iota\n68\t\t// ConsentReasonNoBackfill is --no-backfill.\n69\t\tConsentReasonNoBackfill\n70\t\t// ConsentReasonNoSessions is a repo with nothing recorded yet.\n71\t\tConsentReasonNoSessions\n72\t\t// ConsentReasonNoAgent is sessions present and no CLI able to read them.\n73\t\tConsentReasonNoAgent\n74\t\t// ConsentReasonFlagYes is --yes.\n75\t\tConsentReasonFlagYes\n76\t\t// ConsentReasonNoTTY is a non-interactive stdin, where silence is not\n77\t\t// consent.\n78\t\tConsentReasonNoTTY\n79\t\t// ConsentReasonAccepted is a human who answered yes.\n80\t\tConsentReasonAccepted\n81\t\t// ConsentReasonDeclined is a human who answered no.\n82\t\tConsentReasonDeclined\n83\t\n84\t\t// The four below are reached BEFORE consent is asked, so they are not\n85\t\t// consent decisions at all -- they are the reasons the question never\n86\t\t// came up. They live in this enum because the short form needs one typed\n87\t\t// answer to \"why was nothing distilled\", and inventing a second enum for\n88\t\t// half of it would just move the matching problem.\n89\t\n90\t\t// ConsentReasonPaused is `brain stop`: background work is paused, and\n91\t\t// re-running setup will skip again. The remedy is `start`.\n92\t\tConsentReasonPaused\n93\t\t// ConsentReasonAlreadyDistilled is a re-run with nothing pending.\n94\t\tConsentReasonAlreadyDistilled\n95\t\t// ConsentReasonAlreadyRunning is a backfill already in flight. Reporting\n96\t\t// this as \"skipped\" contradicts the machine's actual state.\n97\t\tConsentReasonAlreadyRunning\n98\t\t// ConsentReasonNoExecutable is an unresolvable path to this binary, so\n99\t\t// nothing could be spawned.\n100\t\tConsentReasonNoExecutable\n101\t)\n102\t\n103\t// ConsentOutcome is the decision and why it was reached.\n104\ttype ConsentOutcome struct {\n105\t\t// Spend is the answer.\n106\t\tSpend bool\n107\t\t// Reason is always set, including when Spend is true. It is what the\n108\t\t// settled phase line says.\n109\t\tReason string\n110\t\t// Why is the same decision as a value, for callers that must branch.\n111\t\tWhy ConsentReason\n112\t\t// Prompted reports whether a human was actually asked. A test asserting\n113\t\t// \"CI does not block\" asserts on this, not on the answer.\n114\t\tPrompted bool\n115\t}\n116\t\n117\t// DefaultResumeCommand is the command printed when a distill is skipped.\n118\tconst DefaultResumeCommand = \"entire brain distill\"\n119\t\n120\t// Consent decides whether phase 4 may spend.\n121\t//\n122\t// Order is load bearing. The three \"spending is impossible\" checks come first,\n123\t// so --yes in a repo with no sessions and no agent reports the truth instead of\n124\t// claiming it spent. Then the flags, then the terminal. The reader `in` is\n125\t// touched on exactly one path: a real prompt on a real terminal.\n126\tfunc Consent(req ConsentRequest, in io.Reader, out io.Writer, r *Renderer) ConsentOutcome {\n127\t\tresume := req.ResumeCommand\n128\t\tif strings.TrimSpace(resume) == \"\" {\n129\t\t\tresume = DefaultResumeCommand\n130\t\t}\n131\t\n132\t\tswitch {\n133\t\t// Nothing to distill comes FIRST, ahead of --no-backfill. The flag\n134\t\t// declines work; it cannot decline work that does not exist, and saying\n135\t\t// \"not distilled (--no-backfill)\" to someone whose repo has no captured\n136\t\t// sessions reports a decision instead of explaining the state. The state\n137\t\t// is that there is nothing here yet, and that is not a problem -- it is\n138\t\t// what every repository looks like before its first agent session.\n139\t\tcase req.Sessions <= 0:\n140\t\t\treturn ConsentOutcome{Reason: \"no sessions to distill; the brain is queryable now\", Why: ConsentReasonNoSessions}\n141\t\tcase req.Override == OverrideNo:\n142\t\t\treturn ConsentOutcome{Reason: \"not distilled (--no-backfill); start later: \" + resume, Why: ConsentReasonNoBackfill}\n143\t\tcase req.Agent == \"\":\n144\t\t\treturn ConsentOutcome{Reason: \"no agent CLI on PATH, nothing can distill; \" + RemedyAgent, Why: ConsentReasonNoAgent}\n145\t\tcase req.Override == OverrideYes:\n146\t\t\treturn ConsentOutcome{Spend: true, Reason: \"distilling \" + plural(req.Sessions, \"session\") + \" (--yes)\", Why: ConsentReasonFlagYes}\n147\t\tcase !req.TTY:\n148\t\t\t// Not a prompt, not a read, not a wait: one line and a default.\n149\t\t\treturn ConsentOutcome{Reason: \"not distilled: no terminal to ask, and silence is not consent; run \" + resume + \" or pass --yes\", Why: ConsentReasonNoTTY}\n150\t\t}\n151\t\n152\t\twritePrompt(out, r, req)\n153\t\tanswer, prompted := askTwice(in, out, r)\n154\t\tif answer {\n155\t\t\treturn ConsentOutcome{Spend: true, Reason: \"distilling \" + plural(req.Sessions, \"session\") + \", newest first\", Why: ConsentReasonAccepted, Prompted: prompted}\n156\t\t}\n157\t\treturn ConsentOutcome{Reason: \"not distilled; the brain is queryable now, start later: \" + resume, Why: ConsentReasonDeclined, Prompted: prompted}\n158\t}\n159\t\n160\t// writePrompt paints the block the operator is answering. It uses the same\n161\t// gutter as every phase line, with the glyph column left blank: a question is\n162\t// not an outcome and must not wear an outcome's tick.\n163\tfunc writePrompt(out io.Writer, r *Renderer, req ConsentRequest) {\n164\t\tif out == nil {\n165\t\t\treturn\n166\t\t}\n167\t\tbullet := \" \" + r.Bullet() + \" \"\n168\t\tagent := \"Agent: \" + req.Agent\n169\t\tif req.Model != \"\" {\n170\t\t\tagent += bullet + \"model: \" + req.Model\n171\t\t}\n172\t\tif req.Effort != \"\" {\n173\t\t\tagent += bullet + \"effort: \" + req.Effort\n174\t\t}\n175\t\tlines := []Line{\n176\t\t\t{Title: PhaseFacts.Title(), Text: plural(req.Sessions, \"session\") + \" can be distilled into durable facts.\", Accent: PhaseFacts.Accent()},\n177\t\t\t{Text: agent, Accent: PhaseFacts.Accent()},\n178\t\t\t{Text: \"Estimated: ~\" + plural(req.Sessions, \"agent call\") + \", newest first, resumable.\", Accent: PhaseFacts.Accent()},\n179\t\t\t{Blank: true},\n180\t\t}\n181\t\tfor _, line := range lines {\n182\t\t\tfmt.Fprintln(out, r.Line(line))\n183\t\t}\n184\t}\n185\t\n186\t// question is the prompt itself. \"[y/N]\" is not decoration: the capital is the\n187\t// default, and it is the default.\n188\tconst question = \"Distill now? [y/N]\"\n189\t\n190\t// askTwice reads an answer, re-asking ONCE on something unrecognisable and\n191\t// defaulting to No after that. Two chances is the whole budget: a loop here is\n192\t// a different way of blocking a pipeline.\n193\tfunc askTwice(in io.Reader, out io.Writer, r *Renderer) (bool, bool) {\n194\t\tif in == nil {\n195\t\t\treturn false, false\n196\t\t}\n197\t\treader := bufio.NewReader(in)\n198\t\tfor attempt := 0; attempt < 2; attempt++ {\n199\t\t\t// Printed with a trailing space Line would have trimmed: the cursor has to\n200\t\t\t// sit clear of the \"]\" or the answer reads as part of the question.\n201\t\t\tfmt.Fprint(out, r.Line(Line{Text: question, Accent: PhaseFacts.Accent()})+\" \")\n202\t\t\tline, err := reader.ReadString('\\n')\n203\t\t\tanswer := strings.ToLower(strings.TrimSpace(line))\n204\t\t\tif err != nil && answer == \"\" {\n205\t\t\t\t// EOF, a closed stdin, an interrupt that shut the pipe: No, with a\n206\t\t\t\t// newline so the next line does not land beside the prompt.\n207\t\t\t\tfmt.Fprintln(out)\n208\t\t\t\treturn false, true\n209\t\t\t}\n210\t\t\tswitch answer {\n211\t\t\tcase \"y\", \"yes\":\n212\t\t\t\treturn true, true\n213\t\t\tcase \"\", \"n\", \"no\":\n214\t\t\t\treturn false, true\n215\t\t\t}\n216\t\t\tif attempt == 0 {\n217\t\t\t\tfmt.Fprintln(out, r.Line(Line{Text: \"Please answer y or n.\", Accent: PhaseFacts.Accent()}))\n218\t\t\t}\n219\t\t\tif err != nil {\n220\t\t\t\tfmt.Fprintln(out)\n221\t\t\t\treturn false, true\n222\t\t\t}\n223\t\t}\n224\t\treturn false, true\n225\t}\n226\t\n\nNote: /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-relnotes/internal/cli/doctor_actionable_test.go was read before the last conversation was summarized, but the contents are too large to include. Use Read tool if you need to access it.\n\nNote: /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-relnotes/internal/cli/setup.go was read before the last conversation was summarized, but the contents are too large to include. Use Read tool if you need to access it.\n\nNote: /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-relnotes/internal/cli/install_ux_test.go was read before the last conversation was summarized, but the contents are too large to include. Use Read tool if you need to access it.\n\nNote: /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-relnotes/internal/cli/hook_cmd.go was read before the last conversation was summarized, but the contents are too large to include. Use Read tool if you need to access it.\n\nThe following tools just became available and are ready to use:\nmcp__claude_ai_Claude_Docs__batch\nmcp__claude_ai_Claude_Docs__guide\nmcp__claude_ai_