{"parentUuid":"28c780eb-ff99-47b0-9ede-a1d14e0580cb","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgBfLiMW8kzsRURCzVij1","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":373,"cache_read_input_tokens":144936,"output_tokens":2789,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":238},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":373,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2789,"cache_read_input_tokens":144936,"cache_creation_input_tokens":373,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":373},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":3252,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","serverClassifierRequest":"15810f01-e3f6-45d5-93f4-7edc67a6ff1d","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgBfLhyvVsGEPQ1uzP5yg","requestRef":"ce260286-294a-4d19-a42d-55d22a6fdf0b","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5[1m]","type":"assistant","uuid":"f43c3cc6-6291-4fd8-9338-9342208865d8","timestamp":"2026-10-19T13:18:40.171Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"60a744a6-1b89-494f-a7de-f94ff9566958","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/cli","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","version":"2.1.301","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floofy-discovering-bachman"}
{"parentUuid":"f43c3cc6-6291-4fd8-9338-9342208865d8","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgBfLiMW8kzsRURCzVij1","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Both answers, then the fix.\n\n## 1. Are the two related? No.\n\n| | ashtom's first message | ashtom's second message (the one you care about) |\n|---|---|---|\n| repo | `entire-graph` | `entire-brain` |\n| subsystem | `internal/sem` indexer | fact **locus / file-anchor** extraction |\n| what | wall-clock ceiling so a hostile repo can't pin the indexer (DoS) | a regex that shreds hyphenated paths |\n\nOnly thing they share is that a security/review loop surfaced both. Different repos, different code, no causal link. Answer him separately.\n\n## 2. Your message\n\n```\nlast week:\n\nfinished the P0 Local Brain fix loop — every open brain PR reviewed, every trail\nfinding resolved and re-verified by weakening the guard\nlanded the entire-graph launch stack on main (39 trails) after the review pass\nsetup/doctor/status output rebuilt: short-form by default, and every printed\nremedy is now something the reader can actually run\ntwo security assessments closed (fast-xml-parser CVE, node-llama-cpp criticals)\n\nentire-brain\n• :review: Doctor warns when the install sits in a directory the OS may delete — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/315\n• :review: Setup output short-form by default, phase view behind --verbose — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/314\n• :review: Six compatibility aliases hidden from the advertised MCP surface — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/313\n• :review: A recorded component failure ages out once it rebuilds — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/312\n• :review: A writer refusing an unknown field is not corruption — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/311\n• :review: brain_recall over MCP, plus a guard against losing a tool again — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/310\n• :review: Pre-push gate settled, two env-only failures named — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/309\n• :review: Semantic provider schema 1.3 ingested in full — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/308\n• :review: Seven-phase setup UI, capability block, distill consent — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/287\n• :review: A repo with no captured sessions is no longer reported broken — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/286\n• :review: Provider failure summarised instead of dumping the host CLI's help — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/285\n• :review: Test suite gets a deadline above its own runtime — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/267\n• :review: Ollama envelope guard bound by the client, not the writer — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/266\n• :review: Changelog since 0.1.0 and the integration branch for the fix stack — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/265\n• :review: Three remedies the reader could not follow — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/264\n• :review: Remedies rendered in the reader's own dispatch spelling — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/263\n• :review: Printed advice made runnable, escape hatch named — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/262\n• :review: Our own installers stop blocking our own install — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/261\n• :review: Setup and status say what is true on a first run — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/260\n• :review: Bundle says what sharing a brain costs, at the moment it costs it — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/259\n• :review: Memory prepass says why it failed, stops retrying what cannot change — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/258\n• :review: Setup makes the brain discoverable and remembers what was declined — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/257\n• :review: Doctor prints only what a reader can act on — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/256\n• :review: Connect fails loudly when the hosted binding cannot be resolved — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/255\n• :review: Retrieval returns output an agent can accept, and discloses what was dropped — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/242\n• :review: Distill timeout configurable, nested-repo trap named — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/241\n• :merged: Brain stops colliding with concurrent git, stalling on a dirty tree, ignoring local models — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/246\n\nentire-graph\n• :merged: Graph launch stack landed on current main — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-graph/trails/262\n• :merged: Committed-tree caches reused across queries, worktrees and clones — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-graph/trails/243\n• :merged: Go router group prefix fixed point bounded (hang on labstack/echo) — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-graph/trails/226\n• :merged: Declaration-aware output and Go route analysis — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-graph/trails/236\n• :merged: Exact corpus-wide IDF statistics — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-graph/trails/214\n• :merged: Agent output no longer depends on measured latency — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-graph/trails/222\n• :merged: Multi-pattern git grep hang fixed, git children killed on signal — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-graph/trails/220\n• :merged: Every relation labelled EXTRACTED, INFERRED or AMBIGUOUS — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-graph/trails/195\n• :merged: Savings unfloored, only pipeline heads classified, writes detected — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-graph/trails/200\n• :merged: Guide asks for --format agent, ~2.9x cheaper per query — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-graph/trails/197\n• :merged: Opt-in prompt-time graph context hook for Claude Code — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-graph/trails/240\n• :merged: Untracked nested worktrees excluded from the corpus — https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-graph/trails/203\n```\n\nTwo notes on it: entire-graph was 39 merged trails last week, I listed the headline plus 11 — say the word and I'll paste the full set. And cli #2292 (`investigate`/`review` error hints) has **no trail**, so I left it out rather than link a PR.\n\nNow the fix."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":373,"cache_read_input_tokens":144936,"output_tokens":2789,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":238},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":373,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2789,"cache_read_input_tokens":144936,"cache_creation_input_tokens":373,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":373},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"15810f01-e3f6-45d5-93f4-7edc67a6ff1d","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgBfLhyvVsGEPQ1uzP5yg","requestRef":"ce260286-294a-4d19-a42d-55d22a6fdf0b","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5[1m]","type":"assistant","uuid":"f6eaa645-db3f-4aa2-a7f1-6322efaed130","timestamp":"2026-10-19T13:19:04.928Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"60a744a6-1b89-494f-a7de-f94ff9566958","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/cli","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","version":"2.1.301","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floofy-discovering-bachman"}
